expr main <([has, have, had] [already, just, never, ever, still] did), (did)>

let message "Use the past participle `done` here."
let description "After `have`, `has` or `had`, the verb needs its past participle: `done`."
let kind "Grammar"
let becomes "done"
let strategy "MatchCase"

test "She has already did it." "She has already done it."
test "She have just did it." "She have just done it."
test "She had never did it." "She had never done it."
test "She has just did it." "She has just done it."
test "She have already did it." "She have already done it."
test "She had already did it." "She had already done it."
test "She has never did it." "She has never done it."
test "She have never did it." "She have never done it."
test "She has still did it." "She has still done it."
test "She had just did it." "She had just done it."
test "She have ever did it." "She have ever done it."
test "She has ever did it." "She has ever done it."
test "They have already did twice." "They have already done twice."

allows "She has already done it."
allows "They have just done it."
allows "She did it yesterday."
allows "He already did it."
allows "We never did it."
allows "She has finished."
